Expose native texture view and sampler handles to YUP compute passes.

- source/renderer/ore/metal/ore_sampler_metal.hpp: Ore Metal sampler: expose the native MTLSamplerState, so YUP compute passes can bind samplers with setSamplerState
- source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_texture_d3d11.hpp: Ore D3D11 texture view: expose the native SRV, so YUP compute passes can bind sampled textures and build storage UAVs
- source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_sampler_d3d11.hpp: Ore D3D11 sampler: expose the native sampler state, so YUP compute passes can bind samplers with CSSetSamplers
- source/renderer/ore/vulkan/ore_texture_vulkan.hpp: Ore Vulkan TextureVulkan: expose the image, its tracked layout and its written subresources, so compute work recorded outside ore can transition it and report back
- source/renderer/ore/vulkan/ore_texture_vulkan.hpp: Ore Vulkan TextureViewVulkan: expose the image view for descriptors written outside ore
- source/renderer/ore/vulkan/ore_sampler_vulkan.hpp: Ore Vulkan SamplerVulkan: expose the sampler for descriptors written outside ore
- source/renderer/ore/wgpu/ore_texture_wgpu.hpp: Ore WebGPU TextureViewWGPU: public accessor for the native view so compute passes can bind it
- source/renderer/ore/wgpu/ore_sampler_wgpu.hpp: Ore WebGPU SamplerWGPU: public accessor for the native sampler so compute passes can bind it

